Carry the PyroWave pacing hints in the stream configuration. pyrowaveLinkMbps is this
client's own wired-link speed toward the host (0 when unknown, Wi-Fi or cellular) and
pyrowavePaceMbps a loss-free pace found by calibration (0 when there is none). Both use the
names and meaning of Nonary's moonlight-common-c, so a PyroWave host that reads them paces a
client behind a slower network port the same way for either client. android_sdp.c sends them
as x-ss-video[0].pyrowaveLinkMbps and x-ss-video[0].pyrowavePaceMbps when above zero.
Independent of the other patches; add it at the end of the list.

diff --git a/src/Limelight.h b/src/Limelight.h
index 22bee46..ed67a46 100644
--- a/src/Limelight.h
+++ b/src/Limelight.h
@@ -100,6 +100,15 @@ typedef struct _STREAM_CONFIGURATION {
     // in /launch and /resume requests.
     char remoteInputAesKey[16];
     char remoteInputAesIv[16];
+
+    // Routed client wired-link speed in Mbps, used by PyroWave host pacing.
+    // Zero means unknown; other codecs do not advertise this value.
+    int pyrowaveLinkMbps;
+
+    // Highest frame pace in Mbps that calibration kept within its loss limit.
+    // The host paces PyroWave frames at this rate instead of its default
+    // pacing. Zero means no calibrated pace.
+    int pyrowavePaceMbps;
 } STREAM_CONFIGURATION, *PSTREAM_CONFIGURATION;
 
 // Use this function to zero the stream configuration when allocated on the stack or heap
